en a baby was  born that people suspected was a stray  god they were banished then one of their  souls died and they became monsters  often with feathers and blue or gray  skin who transformed into alles to suck  the blood of their victims the Strega is  one of the most dangerous creatures in  Polish folklore and it's not easy to get  rid of them some people claim that  cutting off a Stricker's head and  burying it far away from the body will  get the job done although burying one  face down with a sickle around its neck  is said to work to the witcher's fourth  episode of banquets bastards and burials  is based on the Brothers Grimm story  Hans my hedgehog in that story a child  named Hans is born with the legs of a  human and the body and head of a  hedgehog years after his family casts  him out  Hans runs across two lost kings in the  forest Hans offers to help them find  their way but for a price  each ruler needs to give Hans the first  thing that greets the King at the royal  court upon his arrival home that ends up  being the princess meaning Hans gets a  beautiful wife for his trouble Hans and  Unni the curse night in The Witcher  dipper and a few subtle ways while  Dooney is as big as a man Hans is more  Hedgehog size he rides a rooster like a  horse and is often mistaken for an  animal further Dooney simply transforms  into a human Hans his shift is a lot  more gruesome not only does he  physically shed his Hedgehog skin but  after throwing it into the fire his new  human skin is charred black requiring  the aid of a local healer the dryads of  broeckel on forests don't mess around  forced into hiding by humans and  monsters they fearsomely protect their  land from intruders they shoot series  friend ara before he can even reach the  woods they force all newcomers to drink  the water of broke alone which kills  anyone who harbors ill will against the  forest and makes anyone who doesn't  slowly forget their past accordingly the  witcher's dryads dress an a